    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40814" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί-σημον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>distinguishing</i>
			<i>mark, device, badge</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.195
			</span></i>; <i>badge</i> or <i>bearing</i> on a shield, v.l.
				in
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				9.74
			</span></i>; <i>ensign</i> or <i>flag</i> (or <i>figurehead</i>)
			of a ship, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				8.88
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				17
			</span></i>; <i>device</i> on a coin, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; on a signet, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				2588.3
			</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>); <i>serial number,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PPetr.
				3p.203
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίσημα, τά</span>, <i>hieroglyphics</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				56.64
			</span></i> (Canopus, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. generally, <i>mark</i>,
			<i>imprint</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ὁπλῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ichn.</u>
					102
				</span></i>
			.</div>
